    34	#    * {0,1,4,6,8}:
    35	#      - original task deletes it because it contains every shown legend color;
    36	#      - D15-only complement-ALL keeps it because it contains no hidden targets;
    37	#      - this combo keeps it because touching any exclusion color is enough to survive.
    38	#    The visible effect is therefore: deleted objects use only colors absent from the legend, while any
    39	#    object that includes a shown legend color stays.
    40	# b) Complexity calibration:
    41	#    The two constituent changes compose into a double negation. Operationally, the erase test collapses
    42	#    to "component color set has no overlap with the shown legend colors". That means the generator must
    43	#    do extra work so the samples do not look like a trivial D1-only variant. We force two witness roles:
    44	#    - one deleted component that uses only a proper subset of the hidden target colors; this differs from
    45	#      the D15-only complement-ALL behavior and makes the D1 inversion visible after complementing;
    46	#    - one kept component that contains all 4 shown legend colors; this differs from the original task and
    47	#      makes it obvious that the shown colors are exclusions/protective colors rather than deletion colors.
    48	#    When there is room for a second deleted object, it contains all 3 hidden targets so the full target
    49	#    complement is also easy to spot across a few examples.
    50	# c) Implicit-assumption audit:
    51	#    _bg_boundary() still relies on the outer frame being mostly background; the generator does not force
    52	#    every candidate to satisfy this, so candidates that confuse border-based background detection are
    53	#    rejected during verification instead of being emitted.
    54	#    _find_legend() still relies on the smallest top-left corner frame whose bottom and right edges share
    55	#    one non-bg color; the legend geometry is unchanged, so this remains valid.
    56	#    The original solver could safely scan every non-bg component because the legend itself never matched
    57	#    the old ALL rule. Under the new NONE-overlap rule, the border fragment inside the legend square would
    58	#    be erased unless we explicitly skip components contained entirely within the legend box.
